# X-Ray Comparative Study Web Application

A web-based research platform for evaluating chest X-ray cases and comparing AI/VLM-assisted outputs in a controlled academic setting.

This project was created to support research workflows involving chest X-ray image review, annotation, and comparative analysis across selected vision-language / medical imaging models.

---

## Overview

This repository contains the code for a web application designed for research use in the context of chest X-ray evaluation. The platform supports structured review workflows and was built to facilitate comparison, inspection, and analysis of findings produced during the study pipeline.

The system is intended for **academic and research purposes only** and is **not a medical device**. It is **not intended for clinical diagnosis, treatment, or real-world medical decision-making**.

